        "at": "2026-10-23T15:08:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "HOW FAR THEY SEE",
      "narration_text": "One measured detail is worth a look. Receptive field is how many points of the spectrum a single output can see. Our plain CNN, the smallest network, sees nine hundred seventy one points, nearly the whole spectrum. Our ResNet sees four hundred thirty five. The smaller model has the wider view.",
      "shot": {
